{"id":"e1f7dd6b3543a90f01df270b6f3a2a78e46bc96b","url":"https://sourcesli.st/","title":"Download Debian · sourcesli.st","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"sourcesli.st","byline":null,"excerpt":"A quick way to download the right Debian ISO, with its checksum beside it. sourcesli.st is unofficial: built by fnune on the Ultimate Debian Database, and not run by the Debian Project, who publish these images at debian.org. Debian's hardware and bandwidth are paid for by donations.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\">\n\n<header>\n    \n    \n</header>\n\n<main>\n    \n\n\n\n<p>\n    A quick way to download the right Debian ISO, with its checksum beside it.\n    <a href=\"https://code.fnune.com/sourcesli.st/\">sourcesli.st</a> is\nunofficial: built by <a href=\"https://fnune.com\">fnune</a> on the\n<a href=\"https://udd.debian.org/\">Ultimate Debian Database</a>, and not run\nby the Debian Project, who publish these images at\n<a href=\"https://www.debian.org/distrib/\">debian.org</a>.\n    Debian's hardware and bandwidth are paid for by\n<a href=\"https://www.debian.org/donations\">donations</a>.\n</p>\n\n\n\n<section>\n    <div>\n        <h2>64-bit PC</h2>\n        \n        <p><span>looks like this computer</span>\n        \n        <span>Debian 13 (trixie), stable</span>\n    </p></div>\n    <p>\n        Most desktops and laptops, Intel or AMD\n    </p>\n\n    \n    <div>\n        <div>\n            \n            <h3>Live images</h3>\n            \n            <p>Boot from USB without touching your disk. Installs from the same file when you're ready.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <ul>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n<img src=\"/assets/desktops/gnome.webp\" alt=\"Live GNOME\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\">\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>GNOME 48.7</span>\n                        <span>3.8 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Debian's default.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n<img src=\"/assets/desktops/kde.webp\" alt=\"Live KDE Plasma\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\">\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>KDE Plasma 6.3.6</span>\n                        <span>4.2 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Deeply configurable.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n<img src=\"/assets/desktops/xfce.webp\" alt=\"Live Xfce\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\">\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Xfce 4.20.1</span>\n                        <span>3.8 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Light on memory.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n<img src=\"/assets/desktops/cinnamon.webp\" alt=\"Live Cinnamon\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\">\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Cinnamon 6.4.10</span>\n                        <span>4.1 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Linux Mint's desktop.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n<img src=\"/assets/desktops/mate.webp\" alt=\"Live MATE\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\">\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>MATE 1.26.2</span>\n                        <span>4.0 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>The GNOME 2 design.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>No desktop</span>\n                        <span>2.0 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>A console, nothing else.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n    <div>\n        <div>\n            \n            <h3>Just the installer</h3>\n            \n            <p>No desktop to try first. Pick your desktop partway through installing.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <ul>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Network installer</span>\n                        <span>793 MB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Downloads as it installs.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Full DVD</span>\n                        <span>4.0 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Installs with no network.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n</section>\n\n<section>\n    <div>\n        <h2>64-bit ARM</h2>\n        \n        <p><span>Debian 13 (trixie), stable</span>\n    </p></div>\n    <p>\n        Raspberry Pi 4 and later, ARM servers · Live images are 64-bit PC only.\n    </p>\n\n    \n    <div>\n        <p>No desktop to try first. Pick your desktop partway through installing.</p>\n\n        <ul>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Network installer</span>\n                        <span>735 MB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Downloads as it installs.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Full DVD</span>\n                        <span>4.0 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Installs with no network.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n</section>\n\n<section>\n    <div>\n        <h2>32-bit PC</h2>\n        \n        <p><span>Debian 12 (bookworm), oldstable</span>\n    </p></div>\n    <p>\n        Hardware from before roughly 2007 · Debian 13 dropped 32-bit. This is Debian 12, supported until June 2028.\n    </p>\n\n    \n    <div>\n        <p>No desktop to try first. Pick your desktop partway through installing.</p>\n\n        <ul>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Network installer</span>\n                        <span>688 MB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Downloads as it installs.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n            <li>\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                <div>\n                    <p><span>Full DVD</span>\n                        <span>4.0 GB</span>\n                    </p>\n                    <p>Installs with no network.</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                \n            </li>\n            \n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n</section>\n\n\n\n<section>\n    <h2>Popular applications in\n        <span><span></span>stable</span></h2>\n    <p>\n        What counts as an application is our call, not Debian's: graphical programs, minus libraries,\n        desktop plumbing, and whatever a popular metapackage installs for you. Ordered by\n        <a href=\"https://popcon.debian.org/\">popcon</a>, illustrated by\n        <a href=\"https://screenshots.debian.net/\">screenshots.debian.net</a>.\n    </p>\n    \n<ul>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/firefox-esr\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/firefox-esr\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>firefox-esr</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>140.15.0esr-1~deb13u1</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>Mozilla Firefox web browser - Extended Support Release (ESR)</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/graphviz\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/graphviz\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>graphviz</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>2.42.4-3</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>rich set of graph drawing tools</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/ffmpeg\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/ffmpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>ffmpeg</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>7:7.1.5-0+deb13u1</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>Tools for transcoding, streaming and playing of multimedia files</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/gimp\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/gimp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>gimp</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>3.0.4-3+deb13u10</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>GNU Image Manipulation Program</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/thunderbird\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/thunderbird\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>thunderbird</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>1:140.12.0esr-1~deb13u1</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>mail/news client with RSS, chat and integrated spam filter support</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/xterm\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/xterm\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>xterm</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>398-1</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>X terminal emulator</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/chromium\">\n            \n            \n            <img src=\"/screenshots/chromium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n            \n            \n\n            <span>\n                <span>\n                    <span>chromium</span>\n                    \n                    \n                    <span>150.0.7871.181-1~deb13u1</span>\n                    \n                </span>\n                \n                <span>web browser</span>\n            </span>\n        </a>\n    </li>\n    \n    <li>\n        <a href=\"/p/stable/nvidia-settings\">